/* book exam traps: x[n] is not x(nTs) in general. That equality needs ideal sampling; n is an integer count, never a time in seconds. | Brackets and parentheses are not decoration: x(t) is CT, x[n] is DT. Writing x(5) for a sequence loses marks. | The argument of sin and cos is in radians. 0.5π rad is 90°, not 0.5°; a calculator left in degree mode gives wrong answers. | A system is CT or DT by the variable on its input and output, not by its hardware. A filter running on a phone is still a DT system. | x(t) is the whole function; x(2) is one number. Saying 'the signal is 4 V' describes one amplitude, not the signal. */
