/* book: lead: A signal is measured by its size, its repetition and its symmetry. Energy and average power answer how large the signal is over all time. Periodicity answers whether it repeats. Even and odd symmetry answers whether it is a mirror image about zero. These labels decide which transform applies, whether a Fourier series exists, and which terms vanish. You meet them in a mains voltage waveform, a hear */
