/* book exam traps: A periodic finite-amplitude signal is a power signal, not an energy signal. Its energy is infinite, not zero. | Do not confuse zero average value with zero average power. sin(t) has zero mean but P = 1/2 for unit amplitude. | For DT sinusoids, periodic in n needs Ω/(2π) rational. A sampled sine can look periodic on paper but be aperiodic in the sample index. | In the even-part formula, divide by 2. Forgetting the 2 gives twice the even part. | An odd signal must pass through zero at the origin, so x(0) = 0. A signal with x(0) ≠ 0 cannot be purely odd. */
